"Licensor" means edde746, the copyright holder of the Work.

"Work" means everything the Licensor distributes under this license: the source code of the data pipeline, the
trained model weights and their configuration, the databases of titles and age estimates (full and small), and the
documentation, in original or modified form.

"Estimates" means the age suggestions, probabilities and confidence values produced by the Work's model, whether
they come with the Work or are produced by running it.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this license, together with every entity that
controls it, is controlled by it, or is under common control with it.

"FOSS Project" means a software project whose complete source code is publicly available at no charge, under one or
more licenses approved by the Open Source Initiative or listed as free software licenses by the Free Software
Foundation. The Work itself may be part of a FOSS Project and stays under this license.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Work, or of anything built with it, that is intended for or directed towards
commercial advantage or monetary compensation, directly or indirectly. It includes, for example, use in or for:
  (a) a product or service that is sold, licensed for a fee, or offered by subscription;
  (b) a product or service with paid features, paid tiers or in-app purchases, even if the rest is free;
  (c) a product or service that shows advertising, sells or licenses data, or is offered as a paid hosted service;
  (d) the business operations of a for-profit organisation, including internal use;
  (e) consulting, integration or support work done for payment.
Receiving voluntary donations or sponsorship for a FOSS Project is not Commercial Use by itself, as long as no
feature, priority, service or access depends on paying.

